                "template_html": "{{minors_information_TEMPLATE}}",
                "template_html_deselection": "<h2>No processing of personal data of children</h2><p>We do not knowingly collect or solicit personal data from persons under the age of 13. The website is not directed at children under the age of 13. In the event that we learn that we have collected personal data of a child under the age of 13 without parental consent, we will delete that information as quickly as possible. If you believe that we may have personal data from or about a child under 13, please contact us using the contact details outlined in this policy.</p>",
                "title": "Minors/Child",
                "tooltip_html": "<div class=\"f-text-big-content f-text-semibold\"><p>Please note that as per Article 14 of LGPD, children’s personal data can only be collected and processed by you if:</p><ul class=\"mt-3 pl-3\"><li>It is in the best interest of the child pursuant to the LGPD and other relevant legislation in Brazil;</li><li>It is collected and processed through specific and highlighted consent (unless when the collection is necessary for their protection or to contact their parents or the legal representative and as long as the data is used one single time and not stored and under no circumstances shall the data be passed on to third parties without consent);</li><li>If the provision of games, internet applications or other activities is not withheld for not providing consent (unless the personal data is strictly necessary and required).</li><li>Within parental choices and controls, you must highlight procedures for parents and minors to exercise their data subject rights.</li><li>Information should be provided in a simple, clear and accessible manner, taking into account the physical-motor, perceptive, sensorial, intellectual and mental characteristics of the user, using audiovisual resources when appropriate, in order to provide the necessary information to the parents or the legal representative and that is appropriate for the children’s understanding.</li></div>",
