                                    "tooltip_html": "<div class=\"f-text-big-content f-text-semibold\">Compliance with Opt-out Preference Signals</div><br/><div>Please explain to consumers they can activate and use an opt-out preference signal such as the Global Privacy Control (GPC) so that it will be processed and honored by you (i.e., whether the signal applies to the device, browser, consumer account, and/or offline sales, and in what circumstances will detection work etc.)</div><br/><div>It is also important to note that as per CPRA Proposed Regulations § 7025 (f), frictionless compliance with an opt-out preference signal means:</div><ol class=\"mt-3 pl-3\"><li>You do not charge a fee or require any valuable consideration if the consumer uses an opt-out preference signal.</li><li>You do not change the consumer’s experience with the product or service offered by the business for using an opt-out preference signal.</li><li>You do not display a notification, pop-up, text, graphic, animation, sound, video, or any interstitial content in response to the opt-out preference signal.</li></ol>"
