            "title": "Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA) Rights",
            "tooltip_html": "<div class=\"f-text-big-content f-text-semibold\">PIPEDA applies to you if:</div><ol class=\"mt-3 pl-3\"><li>You are a for profit business that collects, uses or discloses personal information in the course of a commercial activity across Canada<ul><li>However, if you operate entirely within Alberta British Columbia, or Quebec - since these provinces have their own privacy laws - PIPEDA does not apply to you. Unless the personal information your organization manages crosses provincial or national borders, in which case PIPEDA shall apply to you.</li></ul></li><li>You are a federally regulated entity i.e a federal works, undertakings or businesses (FWUB) in Canada</li><li>You match condition (1) or (2) and do not fall into any one of these exceptions:<ul><li>You are a government institution to which the Privacy Act applies;</li><li>You are an individual handling personal information for personal reasons;</li><li>You are an organization handling personal information for journalistic, artistic or literary purposes.</li></ul></li></ol>",
