                "title": "California Consumer Protection Act (CCPA) Rights",
                "tooltip_html": "<div class=\"f-text-big-content f-text-semibold\">Does CCPA apply to you?</div><br/><div>CCPA applies to you if:</div><ol class=\"mt-3 pl-3\"><li>You are a for profit business;</li><li>You do business in the State of California (this means you provide or market goods and services to residents of California);</li><li>You match anyone of these requirements:<ul><li>You have an annual gross revenue of in excess of $25,000,000 ($25 million).</li><li>You annually buy/sell or receive/share (for commercial purposes), alone or in combination, the personal information of 100,000 or more consumers or households.</li><li>You derive 50% or more of your annual revenue from selling consumers’ personal information.</li></ul><li>You match condition (1), (2) and (3) but do not match any one of the following exceptions:</li></li><ul><li>You are a covered entity or business associate managing protected health information under HIPAA/HITECH;</li><li>You are a provider of health care managing medical information under the Confidentiality of Medical Information Act;</li><li>You are collecting information as part of a clinical trial subject to the Federal Policy for the Protection of Human Subjects, also known as the Common Rule;</li><li>You are collecting, maintaining, disclosing, selling, communicating, or using any personal information for the purposes of ascertaining a consumer’s credit worthiness, credit standing, credit capacity, character, general reputation, personal characteristics, or mode of living under the Fair Credit Reporting Act;</li><li>You are a financial institution collecting, processing, selling disclosing personal information under federal Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act or the California Financial Information Privacy Act;</li><li>You are collecting, processing, selling, or disclosing personal information pursuant to the Driver’s Privacy Protection Act of 1994.</li></ul></li></ol>",
