                "title": "California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA) Rights",
                "tooltip_html": "<div class=\"f-text-big-content f-text-semibold\">Does CPRA apply to you?</div><br/><div>CPRA applies if your &#34;business&#34;:</div><ol class=\"mt-3 pl-3\"><li>Is a for-profit business;</li><li>Does business in the state of California (this means it provides goods and services - or markets them - to residents of California.</li><li>And meets any one of the following requirements:<ul><li>Has made annual gross revenues in excess of twenty-five million dollars ($25,000,000) in the preceding calendar year.</li><li>Annually buys/sells/shares, alone or in combination, personal information of 100,000 or more consumers or households.</li><li>Derives 50 percent or more of its annual revenues from selling, or sharing consumers&#39; personal information.</li></ul><li>You match condition (1), (2) and (3) but do not match any one of the following exceptions:</li></li><ul><li>You are a covered entity or business associate managing protected health information under HIPAA/HITECH;</li><li>You are a provider of health care managing medical information under the Confidentiality of Medical Information Act;</li><li>You are collecting information as part of a clinical trial or other biomedical research study subject to the Federal Policy for the Protection of Human Subjects, also known as the Common Rule or good clinical practice guidelines issued by the International Council for Harmonisation or the human subject protection requirements of the United States Food and Drug Administration provided that the information is not sold or shared in an inconsistent manner without the data subject’s consent;</li><li>You are collecting, maintaining, disclosing, selling, communicating, or using any personal information for the purposes of ascertaining a consumer’s credit worthiness, credit standing, credit capacity, character, general reputation, personal characteristics, or mode of living under the Fair Credit Reporting Act;</li><li>You are collecting, processing, selling disclosing personal information under the Federal Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act or the California Financial Information Privacy Act or the Federal Farm Credit Act of 1971;</li><li>You are collecting, processing, selling, or disclosing personal information pursuant to the Driver’s Privacy Protection Act of 1994.</li></ul></li></ol>",
